<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Paulinus of York</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 644</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Paulinus was a Roman missionary sent to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> in 601 to join Augustine's mission, and the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of York. He went to Northumbria with Æthelburh of Kent on her marriage to King Edwin, whom he baptised at York in 627, and preached in Deira, Bernicia and Lindsey, where he built a stone church at Lincoln. After Edwin's death in 633 he fled to Kent and ended his life as bishop of Rochester.</p></div>
